Short Circuit Operator :
1) In the case of logical AND if the first arg is '0' that is false , 
we no need to execute the second arg, we can give the result directly as zero(0);
2) In the case of logical OR, if first arg is true,then  no need to check the second arg directly we can give the result as one (1).
3) In the case o logical && ,logical || based on the first arg , we are skipping the execution of the 2nd argument
Hense, logical && || are called as Short Circuit Operators 

